    <defName>RM_Gorrask</defName>
    <label>gorrask</label>
    <description>Legend on this rock says a stone-crab grew so vast and so old that it no longer fits inside any canyon it did not carve itself. Whatever the truth of that, a gorrask this big has never needed to hurry: it moves once, settles for a season, and the pool truce holds around it exactly as it holds around everything smaller. Its shell is old enough that whole weep-mat colonies have taken root along the seams.</description>
